{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13411-pacts-assets-and-transferrable","id":13411,"title":"Pacts, Assets, and \"Transferrable\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T08:46:26-08:00","id":13411,"title":"Pacts, Assets, and \"Transferrable\"","content":"So far I've been getting a huge kick out of reading over the Demon draft that was made available. I do have a few questions about pacts and what can be done with them.<br /> <br /> 1) The &quot;Where Does The Money Come From&quot; gives examples of what can be granted to a mortal as an Asset and quickly translates game world terminology to mechanics terms (Riches = Resources, Friends = Allies etc) but then mentions that one of the things that can be granted is Health, which is translated as Stamina. Is this referring to something like the &quot;Iron Stamina&quot; merit or is there a way to actually grant attributes / health levels? Similarly, things like youth, curing diseases / conditions, love, and other such nebulous things that were touched on vaguely throughout the book, how do these go?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you transfer a cover element to a mortal as part of a pact? Let's say Bob has always had an infatuation with Mary. Mary's boyfriend, Sam, just made a pact with a Demon, transferring his relationship with Mary to the Demon in exchange for something. Can that same Demon transfer his new relationship with Mary to Bob in exchange for something? How would that work out?<br /> <br /> 3) Is it possible to transfer cover elements from cover to cover? Particularly patchwork covers. Using the Mary example, let's say the Demon is building a nice cover as &quot;Mr. Brown the Business Tycoon&quot; and has her all lined up to be part of that. Before it becomes a real (5+ cover) the Demon decides that he really wants to be &quot;Mr. Blue the News Channel Cameraman&quot;. Is he pretty much SOL on that front or does Mary suddenly remember that she's been in a relationship with a Cameraman this whole time?<br /> <br /> There are other questions that can come with these, most of which involving various forms of psychological inhumanity and the like (Demon flesh trader, creating temporary &quot;love&quot; pacts by farming out a &quot;long term relationship&quot; element that they picked up for days at a time, for a start) but these are the cornerstones of many such questions.<br /> <br /> Thanks people.<br /> Amazing book, seriously <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:57:57-08:00","id":13459,"title":"","content":"I think references to Stamina are from part of the book that has been dropped. As for things like youth, love or more negligible things, I have no idea. Personally I think there should be an option for a free use of an Embed/Exploit as a possible mortal benefit. There also should be an option for services rendered by the demon. It may be possile to take &quot;negative space&quot; as life aspects as well, thus taking someone's perpetual loneliness so they in turn find love, ut that would require careful adjudication - Covers are meant to provide identities and negatives don't really establish things the same way.<br /> <br /> By strict rules as written, Cover elements can only benefit a demon. That said, it should be possible to do so because the story potential is too awesome not to. You would need the permission of all participants, and you'd get no Cover experience, but it should be possible to forge a contract among multiple parties. As a side note, while a demon cannot lie as part of a contract, there doesn't seem to be any such compulsion on a mortal accomplice.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm not entirely sure how transferring patchwork and souls pacts even work. Does the original demon lose the experience spent and the new holder gain it? What happens to the original's Cover?<br /> <br /> As for trading Cover elements from Cover to Cover, I believe that defeats the purpose. Cover experience gained really should apply to one Cover and one Cover only. At the very least, it may be possible but a good way to wind up being investigated.<br /> <br /> So that's my take at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:38:56-08:00","id":13489,"title":"","content":"After some reading, I think love could be handled with the &quot;True Friend&quot; Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:50:14-08:00","id":13493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13411-pacts-assets-and-transferrable?p=13489#post13489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After some reading, I think love could be handled with the &quot;True Friend&quot; Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly would fit the equal pricing between Greater Assets and Greater Cover Pacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}